And quite honestly, it was a blessing in disguise.

1277
00:41:49.110 --> 00:41:50.440
And you know, there's always a silver lining,

1278
00:41:50.440 --> 00:41:52.260
people say that, but in this case there was,

1279
00:41:52.260 --> 00:41:54.820
'cause it's like you said, those pushups in those years,

1280
00:41:54.820 --> 00:41:57.530
I didn't go back on for about three more years,

1281
00:41:57.530 --> 00:41:59.950
and those three years I did a huge volume of shows,

1282
00:41:59.950 --> 00:42:01.310
and I got better and better.

1283
00:42:01.310 --> 00:42:02.740
The more you do it, the more you iterate,

1284
00:42:02.740 --> 00:42:05.010
the more you see it works, and kind of my persona developed.

1285
00:42:05.010 --> 00:42:08.640
And when I went back in, I went in not caring.

1286
00:42:08.640 --> 00:42:11.437
I was gonna go in two years later, but it was so cold out,

1287
00:42:11.437 --> 00:42:14.340
it was 15 degrees fahrenheit with like a wind chill,

1288
00:42:14.340 --> 00:42:15.790
and I went out there to stand in line,

1289
00:42:15.790 --> 00:42:18.830
and I stood in line for three hours, I was dying,

1290
00:42:18.830 --> 00:42:19.663
and then I had a show.

1291
00:42:19.663 --> 00:42:20.580
I thought I was gonna be done,

1292
00:42:20.580 --> 00:42:21.627
and I had to go do a show, and I'm like,

1293
00:42:21.627 --> 00:42:22.460
"Screw this."

1294
00:42:22.460 --> 00:42:23.637
I told my wife, I'm like,

1295
00:42:23.637 --> 00:42:25.230
"I'm done."

1296
00:42:25.230 --> 00:42:26.180
And I skipped it.

1297
00:42:26.180 --> 00:42:28.010
And then the next year I came back,

1298
00:42:28.010 --> 00:42:29.640
thank God it wasn't that cold,

1299
00:42:29.640 --> 00:42:32.430
and I waited for like seven hours, I did not care.

1300
00:42:32.430 --> 00:42:36.490
I'm not lying to you, I did not care at all what happened,

1301
00:42:36.490 --> 00:42:39.540
I went in there, like I owned the place, and I killed it.

1302
00:42:39.540 --> 00:42:41.310
Because kinda like actors that do auditions,

1303
00:42:41.310 --> 00:42:42.630
you hear about actresses that go in,

1304
00:42:42.630 --> 00:42:43.720
they don't think they're getting the part,

1305
00:42:43.720 --> 00:42:46.970
so they just are so loose, I was so loose, I walked in,

1306
00:42:46.970 --> 00:42:49.517
and then I went in, and then I just cracked jokes, I go,

1307
00:42:49.517 --> 00:42:50.570
"Guys, we don't even need to do this,

1308
00:42:50.570 --> 00:42:52.100
you already found the guy who's gonna win a million bucks."

1309
00:42:52.100 --> 00:42:54.930
And I was just like, completely just let it go,

1310
00:42:54.930 --> 00:42:56.237
'cause I really didn't think I was getting on,

1311
00:42:56.237 --> 00:42:58.420
and they loved it, and that was it,

1312
00:42:58.420 --> 00:43:00.470
and that was the season that I ended up getting third place.

1313
00:43:00.470 --> 00:43:02.550
It is powerful when you don't care.

1314
00:43:02.550 --> 00:43:05.300
It's the greatest power you have to say no.

1315
00:43:05.300 --> 00:43:10.300
That ability to detach from expectations and results,

1316
00:43:10.580 --> 00:43:14.010
just allows you to flourish in those high pressure moments.

1317
00:43:14.010 --> 00:43:15.663
1000%.
Yeah.

1318
00:43:16.860 --> 00:43:18.360
I can't believe you got third?

1319
00:43:19.520 --> 00:43:22.150
That's a good or bad?
No, I mean,

1320
00:43:22.150 --> 00:43:24.137
I watched your performances, and I was like,

1321
00:43:24.137 --> 00:43:25.260
"Who's better than this?"

1322
00:43:25.260 --> 00:43:26.195
Oh, thanks man.
I don't watch

1323
00:43:26.195 --> 00:43:27.960
the show that much, so I don't know

1324
00:43:27.960 --> 00:43:32.070
who won and got second that year, but I mean,

1325
00:43:32.070 --> 00:43:34.430
you had those people eating out of the palm of your hand.

1326
00:43:34.430 --> 00:43:36.380
I mean, they were going insane.

1327
00:43:36.380 --> 00:43:38.620
And I would imagine it's very difficult

1328
00:43:38.620 --> 00:43:41.360
to thread this needle week in, week out,

1329
00:43:41.360 --> 00:43:43.540
so you have to do six performances, right?

1330
00:43:43.540 --> 00:43:45.350
It's crazy.
And you can't peak

1331
00:43:45.350 --> 00:43:47.620
too early, you can't blow your best stuff-

1332
00:43:47.620 --> 00:43:48.453
You nailed it.
... On the first

1333
00:43:48.453 --> 00:43:52.000
or second one, but it has to get better,

1334
00:43:52.000 --> 00:43:53.090
and it has to be good enough,

1335
00:43:53.090 --> 00:43:55.150
so you're gonna make it to the next round,

1336
00:43:55.150 --> 00:43:58.470
so that's a difficult kind of equation to square.

1337
00:43:58.470 --> 00:43:59.940
The highs and the lows of that show,

1338
00:43:59.940 --> 00:44:00.773
if you ask me the part of my life...

1339
00:44:00.773 --> 00:44:03.220
You know, where you live something that's surreal,

1340
00:44:03.220 --> 00:44:06.890
because you know you lived it, but it happened so quick,

1341
00:44:06.890 --> 00:44:09.247
that it almost feels like it was a dream or a movie.

1342
00:44:09.247 --> 00:44:12.030
The last stages of that show, when you're so in it.

1343
00:44:12.030 --> 00:44:13.530
And obviously other people, some people watch the show,

1344
00:44:13.530 --> 00:44:15.110
some people don't, but when it's your life,

1345
00:44:15.110 --> 00:44:18.860
and you're like there, on a Tuesday, you'll perform live,

1346
00:44:18.860 --> 00:44:20.649
and it was the number one show on TV,

1347
00:44:20.649 --> 00:44:21.482
I don't know if it still is,

1348
00:44:21.482 --> 00:44:23.527
but it's the number one TV show in the country,

1349
00:44:23.527 --> 00:44:25.530
and to some defacto in the world,

1350
00:44:25.530 --> 00:44:28.730
because it's watched on YouTube internationally.

1351
00:44:28.730 --> 00:44:30.090
As soon as you get on that show,

1352
00:44:30.090 --> 00:44:31.600
people call you from all over the world,

1353
00:44:31.600 --> 00:44:33.620
I was called from six continents.

1354
00:44:33.620 --> 00:44:37.480
And so you perform on Tuesday night live,

1355
00:44:37.480 --> 00:44:39.500
which is its own beast, you can't screw anything up.

1356
00:44:39.500 --> 00:44:41.300
There's nothing, it's not edited at all,

1357
00:44:41.300 --> 00:44:43.400
if you screw anything up, you're done.

1358
00:44:43.400 --> 00:44:44.780
The next day on Wednesday night,

1359
00:44:44.780 --> 00:44:48.180
they tell you if you got through, so that Wednesday night,

1360
00:44:48.180 --> 00:44:50.280
you're on like a high that you just can't believe.

1361
00:44:50.280 --> 00:44:53.240
Your skin is like, tingling.

1362
00:44:53.240 --> 00:44:54.930
And then you have maybe five minutes,

1363
00:44:54.930 --> 00:44:57.063
before you walk backstage, and the producer goes,

1364
00:44:57.063 --> 00:44:58.010
"Okay, great.

1365
00:44:58.010 --> 00:44:58.843
Tomorrow morning, we gotta talk

1366
00:44:58.843 --> 00:45:00.750
about what you're doing in six days,

1367
00:45:00.750 --> 00:45:02.936
and we're doing a rehearsal in four days."

1368
00:45:02.936 --> 00:45:04.623
And so it's like-
And how much do

1369
00:45:04.623 --> 00:45:06.053
they need to know ahead of time?

1370
00:45:06.053 --> 00:45:06.886
Everything.
I mean,

1371
00:45:06.886 --> 00:45:08.391
you had mentioned earlier, that you had

1372
00:45:08.391 --> 00:45:09.900
to walk them through it-
They know everything.

1373
00:45:09.900 --> 00:45:11.470
So you have to actually explain to them,

1374
00:45:11.470 --> 00:45:12.573
how you're doing it,

1375
00:45:12.573 --> 00:45:14.010
so they're in on it?
100%.

1376
00:45:14.010 --> 00:45:15.630
The one joy of that show, I call it,

1377
00:45:15.630 --> 00:45:16.610
the emperor has no clothes,

1378
00:45:16.610 --> 00:45:18.740
is when I do almost every other TV show,

1379
00:45:18.740 --> 00:45:20.040
I've got two things working with me.

1380
00:45:20.040 --> 00:45:21.390
I'm trying to fool the audience,

1381
00:45:21.390 --> 00:45:22.960
and entertain the audience at home,

1382
00:45:22.960 --> 00:45:25.340
while also not letting the producer and TV staff,

1383
00:45:25.340 --> 00:45:26.660
know how in the world I'm doing this.

1384
00:45:26.660 --> 00:45:27.857
Most TV shows you'll go to, they'll be like,

1385
00:45:27.857 --> 00:45:29.143
"I have no idea how he just did that."

1386
00:45:29.143 --> 00:45:31.650
Like I did "Ellen" a couple months ago,

1387
00:45:31.650 --> 00:45:33.050
and I did a thing in the audience,

1388
00:45:33.050 --> 00:45:34.490
if somebody wants to watch it, I don't wanna spoil,

1389
00:45:34.490 --> 00:45:36.220
but I did almost like a mass suggestion

1390
00:45:36.220 --> 00:45:38.630
of an entire audience, and at the end of the show,

1391
00:45:38.630 --> 00:45:40.240
I wish you had a clip of "Ellen",

1392
00:45:40.240 --> 00:45:42.677
five seconds after the camera's ended, where I go,

1393
00:45:42.677 --> 00:45:44.480
"Ellen, this is your audience."

1394
00:45:44.480 --> 00:45:46.270
She's done that show for 19 years,

1395
00:45:46.270 --> 00:45:48.410
she understands that there's 250 people in the audience,

1396
00:45:48.410 --> 00:45:50.998
and that I don't have a way to set anything up with them.

1397
00:45:50.998 --> 00:45:52.100
Do you understand?

1398
00:45:52.100 --> 00:45:52.933
She knows, I go,

1399
00:45:52.933 --> 00:45:54.380
"This is your audience, you know."

1400
00:45:54.380 --> 00:45:55.957
And she grabbed me, and she goes,

1401
00:45:55.957 --> 00:45:56.790
"I know that."

1402
00:45:56.790 --> 00:45:58.790
She understands that if you're watching at home,

1403
00:45:58.790 --> 00:45:59.623
you're saying,

1404
00:45:59.623 --> 00:46:00.760
"This is fake, this has to be set up,

1405
00:46:00.760 --> 00:46:02.640
he must have told those people what to do,

1406
00:46:02.640 --> 00:46:03.890
or like done something."

1407
00:46:03.890 --> 00:46:06.830
She knows that those people get loaded in, in a room,

1408
00:46:06.830 --> 00:46:08.320
she comes out, there's a warmup act,

1409
00:46:08.320 --> 00:46:10.680
there is no way to know who's gonna be in that audience,

1410
00:46:10.680 --> 00:46:12.070
do you understand what I'm saying?

1411
00:46:12.070 --> 00:46:14.040
Sure, I mean, I saw the clip.

1412
00:46:14.040 --> 00:46:15.080
Yeah, her reaction.
And I think

1413
00:46:15.080 --> 00:46:18.640
I have a sense of how you led them to that place.

1414
00:46:18.640 --> 00:46:20.010
I hope you try.
And everybody can watch it,

1415
00:46:20.010 --> 00:46:21.870
or maybe we can cut it into this video,

1416
00:46:21.870 --> 00:46:24.211
so people can see part of it.

1417
00:46:24.211 --> 00:46:26.560
Oh my God, Oz, you're amazing.

1418
00:46:26.560 --> 00:46:28.232
Thank you.
You're incredible.

1419
00:46:28.232 --> 00:46:30.504
But there are Easter eggs?

1420
00:46:30.504 --> 00:46:31.928
Oh, I want Easter eggs.
You watch these

1421
00:46:31.928 --> 00:46:34.238
a bunch of times, you can see where,

1422
00:46:34.238 --> 00:46:36.140
a little bit about how you're getting

1423
00:46:36.140 --> 00:46:38.390
them to arrive in the place you want 'em to be.

1424
00:46:38.390 --> 00:46:41.633
Exactly, and so that's the best part.

1425
00:46:41.633 --> 00:46:43.900
Yeah, man, I don't know the "AGT" stuff.

1426
00:46:43.900 --> 00:46:46.360
And I didn't plan ahead, so a lot of people

1427
00:46:46.360 --> 00:46:47.890
that I've talked to, they'll plan ahead.

1428
00:46:47.890 --> 00:46:48.723
I've consulted,

1429
00:46:48.723 --> 00:46:50.790
I've like helped other people that are doing the show,

1430
00:46:50.790 --> 00:46:52.320
'cause once you have an insight track,

1431
00:46:52.320 --> 00:46:53.780
you can be very helpful to them.

1432
00:46:53.780 --> 00:46:56.130
And I've found, time and again, anyone who plans it,

1433
00:46:56.130 --> 00:46:56.963
who's like,

1434
00:46:56.963 --> 00:46:57.796
"I'm gonna do this in my first round,

1435
00:46:57.796 --> 00:46:58.629
this is my second round."

1436
00:46:58.629 --> 00:47:00.074
They don't make it through the first round.

1437
00:47:00.074 --> 00:47:01.420
Like it's like a football player.

1438
00:47:01.420 --> 00:47:02.508
If you are thinking

1439
00:47:02.508 --> 00:47:04.230
about what you're gonna do after you catch the ball,

1440
00:47:04.230 --> 00:47:05.190
how you're gonna run and get a touch down

1441
00:47:05.190 --> 00:47:06.840
you end up dropping the ball.

1442
00:47:06.840 --> 00:47:08.840
So I literally, swear on my life,

1443
00:47:08.840 --> 00:47:10.660
I did not know what I was gonna do the next round,

1444
00:47:10.660 --> 00:47:12.149
all I focused on, 100%,

1445
00:47:12.149 --> 00:47:15.070
putting the best act together I could for this round.

1446
00:47:15.070 --> 00:47:17.810
And I also did in the last three, all original material,

1447
00:47:17.810 --> 00:47:18.760
which a lot of people don't,

1448
00:47:18.760 --> 00:47:20.080
they do the stuff they know kills,

1449
00:47:20.080 --> 00:47:21.480
that they've done hundreds of times.

1450
00:47:21.480 --> 00:47:22.313
I said,

1451
00:47:22.313 --> 00:47:23.146
"If I'm gonna be on this stage,

1452
00:47:23.146 --> 00:47:25.470
I gotta do stuff that's like next level each time,

1453
00:47:25.470 --> 00:47:26.540
and kind of raise the bar."

1454
00:47:26.540 --> 00:47:28.870
So your coming up with new stuff,

1455
00:47:28.870 --> 00:47:31.842
it wasn't like I have six of my best things.

1456
00:47:31.842 --> 00:47:32.890
No.
I'll move

1457
00:47:32.890 --> 00:47:33.723
them around in this way-

1458
00:47:33.723 --> 00:47:34.556
No way.
... And that's

1459
00:47:34.556 --> 00:47:35.389
how this is gonna play out?

1460
00:47:35.389 --> 00:47:37.510
No, like two of them at the beginning,

1461
00:47:37.510 --> 00:47:39.880
were my core act, the audition,

1462
00:47:39.880 --> 00:47:41.410
'cause you audition with something you've already done,

1463
00:47:41.410 --> 00:47:42.980
it would be silly to do something you haven't.

1464
00:47:42.980 --> 00:47:45.060
In fact, the producers, you show them your best thing,

1465
00:47:45.060 --> 00:47:45.893
and they're like,

1466
00:47:45.893 --> 00:47:47.368
"Do that on the first show."

1467
00:47:47.368 --> 00:47:48.939
But the last round, for example,

1468
00:47:48.939 --> 00:47:49.772
I did this thing with chairs,

1469
00:47:49.772 --> 00:47:52.190
and it was kind of wild, where they all sat in chairs.

1470
00:47:52.190 --> 00:47:53.930
I made that up five days before,

1471
00:47:53.930 --> 00:47:56.755
and it was a whirlwind of insanity.

1472
00:47:56.755 --> 00:47:59.340
I hate and love deadlines,

1473
00:47:59.340 --> 00:48:01.420
because that's where I get creativity.

1474
00:48:01.420 --> 00:48:03.420
Three days ago I had a show for a client,

1475
00:48:03.420 --> 00:48:04.930
that's had me three times,

1476
00:48:04.930 --> 00:48:06.710
and they need me to do something different.

1477
00:48:06.710 --> 00:48:10.137
And I complained to my wife endlessly, I'm like,

1478
00:48:10.137 --> 00:48:11.200
"This sucks."

1479
00:48:11.200 --> 00:48:12.110
But I love it.

1480
00:48:12.110 --> 00:48:14.330
Secretly inside, I love the fact that I'm gonna

1481
00:48:14.330 --> 00:48:16.090
have to come up with practically a whole new show.

1482
00:48:16.090 --> 00:48:17.590
The constraints are what pushes

1483
00:48:17.590 --> 00:48:20.260
the outer boundaries of creative expression.

1484
00:48:20.260 --> 00:48:21.560
I love it.
Yeah.

1485
00:48:21.560 --> 00:48:24.620
But how do you come up with this stuff?

1486
00:48:24.620 --> 00:48:26.660
I mean, do you get on the mentalist hotline,

1487
00:48:26.660 --> 00:48:28.180
and call your mentalist bros?

1488
00:48:28.180 --> 00:48:29.520
First of all, there are probably not

1489
00:48:29.520 --> 00:48:31.390
that many of them, right?

1490
00:48:31.390 --> 00:48:34.040
You guys talk to each other, or share trade secrets,

1491
00:48:34.040 --> 00:48:36.883
or is it all proprietary and locked down?

1492
00:48:38.070 --> 00:48:40.930
There's a network of people, it's primarily guys,

1493
00:48:40.930 --> 00:48:41.763
I don't know why.

1494
00:48:41.763 --> 00:48:42.690
There's a ton of Israeli guys too,

1495
00:48:42.690 --> 00:48:43.574
it's so weird, I don't know, what's in the water.

1496
00:48:43.574 --> 00:48:44.407
Really?

1497
00:48:44.407 --> 00:48:46.282
Yeah, there's a guy called (indistinct)?

1498
00:48:46.282 --> 00:48:47.420
(indistinct), who is a good friend of mine,

1499
00:48:47.420 --> 00:48:49.540
there's so many Israelis for some reason, I don't know why.

1500
00:48:49.540 --> 00:48:51.200
Also I know, like David Blaine is Jewish,

1501
00:48:51.200 --> 00:48:52.280
David Copperfield is Jewish,

1502
00:48:52.280 --> 00:48:54.323
I don't know what's in the water, but somehow,

1503
00:48:54.323 --> 00:48:56.580
this religion has been drawn into this profession.

1504
00:48:56.580 --> 00:48:57.413
I don't know how to explain.

1505
00:48:57.413 --> 00:48:58.310
There's plenty that aren't too,

1506
00:48:58.310 --> 00:49:00.250
but I'm just saying it's a weird, I don't know...

1507
00:49:00.250 --> 00:49:03.268
(indistinct), is like one of the original mentalists,

1508
00:49:03.268 --> 00:49:04.130
the guy who used to bend spoons,

1509
00:49:04.130 --> 00:49:06.036
and got debunked on Johnny Carson?

1510
00:49:06.036 --> 00:49:09.720
But there's a network of people I bounce ideas off of,

1511
00:49:09.720 --> 00:49:11.040
and there's sounding boards.

1512
00:49:11.040 --> 00:49:12.960
And there's some elements that I make up,

1513
00:49:12.960 --> 00:49:14.260
a lot of the stuff myself.

1514
00:49:14.260 --> 00:49:16.460
Some of it is kind of, you have a set of tools.

1515
00:49:16.460 --> 00:49:19.180
Think of it as, I'm trying to think of the close thing,

1516
00:49:19.180 --> 00:49:20.013
it's almost like an artist.

1517
00:49:20.013 --> 00:49:21.540
You know, you have watercolors, I have this paint,

1518
00:49:21.540 --> 00:49:24.803
I have this medium, and now how do I put those together?

1519
00:49:24.803 --> 00:49:28.400
Some people use the tools to create the finished product,

1520
00:49:28.400 --> 00:49:30.520
I start with the finished product in my head.

1521
00:49:30.520 --> 00:49:31.770
Like when I did that "Ellen" appearance,

1522
00:49:31.770 --> 00:49:33.800
I knew exactly what I wanted the end to be.

1523
00:49:33.800 --> 00:49:35.900
That moment where an entire audience,

