2032
01:05:40.840 --> 01:05:42.420
Like I've always got a path out

2033
01:05:42.420 --> 01:05:43.620
in my mind of how I'm gonna do this.

2034
01:05:43.620 --> 01:05:46.940
Yeah.
On colossal failures,

2035
01:05:46.940 --> 01:05:49.650
have generally been things that are outside of my control.

2036
01:05:49.650 --> 01:05:52.170
Like for example, I did a show one time,

2037
01:05:52.170 --> 01:05:54.770
God, this was in like South Carolina, or somewhere,

2038
01:05:54.770 --> 01:05:56.740
where it's generally like a corporate event.

2039
01:05:56.740 --> 01:05:59.400
They bring me on stage, they're gonna have a smoke machine,

2040
01:05:59.400 --> 01:06:01.200
didn't know there was gonna be a smoke machine.

2041
01:06:01.200 --> 01:06:02.150
There's gonna be a CEO,

2042
01:06:02.150 --> 01:06:03.810
popping out of a life sized genie lamp,

2043
01:06:03.810 --> 01:06:05.410
didn't know this was gonna happen.

2044
01:06:05.410 --> 01:06:06.613
And just all these things went wrong.

2045
01:06:06.613 --> 01:06:09.170
When the smoke machine didn't stop, there's smoke on stage,

2046
01:06:09.170 --> 01:06:11.620
I can't see the person whose mind I'm trying to read,

2047
01:06:11.620 --> 01:06:12.680
trick goes south.

2048
01:06:12.680 --> 01:06:15.170
Just things where you just leave the stage...

2049
01:06:15.170 --> 01:06:16.650
The worst thing that can ever happen

2050
01:06:16.650 --> 01:06:18.710
is when a TV producer, or the client,

2051
01:06:18.710 --> 01:06:19.543
comes up to you and they go,

2052
01:06:19.543 --> 01:06:20.960
"Oh man, I'm so sorry about that."

2053
01:06:20.960 --> 01:06:21.793
Like, they feel bad,

2054
01:06:21.793 --> 01:06:23.120
'cause they know you're better than this,

2055
01:06:23.120 --> 01:06:26.980
and you're just crushed, because you tanked, and there's,

2056
01:06:26.980 --> 01:06:28.550
I don't know, things like that.

2057
01:06:28.550 --> 01:06:32.350
There's been failures on my part, but, yeah, I don't know,

2058
01:06:32.350 --> 01:06:33.323
there's a few that I can think of,

2059
01:06:33.323 --> 01:06:35.499
that were gut punches, where I left the stage, and I'm like,

2060
01:06:35.499 --> 01:06:36.360
"(indistinct)."

2061
01:06:36.360 --> 01:06:38.210
And generally people feel worse for you,

2062
01:06:38.210 --> 01:06:39.261
they feel okay about...

2063
01:06:39.261 --> 01:06:40.094
Do you understand?

2064
01:06:40.094 --> 01:06:42.080
They feel bad for you, they're not mad at you,

2065
01:06:42.080 --> 01:06:42.913
they're just like,

2066
01:06:42.913 --> 01:06:44.419
"We know you're better than this."

2067
01:06:44.419 --> 01:06:46.510
Yeah.
But yeah.

2068
01:06:46.510 --> 01:06:48.177
Bombing in front of thousands of people.

2069
01:06:48.177 --> 01:06:51.291
But you gotta bomb, it's like a standup comedian,

2070
01:06:51.291 --> 01:06:53.490
you have to know where the edge is, right?

2071
01:06:53.490 --> 01:06:54.820
You have to touch that line,

2072
01:06:54.820 --> 01:06:55.653
or else you're not growing.
And the only way

2073
01:06:55.653 --> 01:06:57.970
to know that is, if you cross it once in a while.

2074
01:06:57.970 --> 01:06:58.803
I love standup.

2075
01:06:58.803 --> 01:07:01.500
Standup comedy is my favorite thing to watch.

2076
01:07:01.500 --> 01:07:03.530
You know how kind of like movie stars wanna be rock stars,

2077
01:07:03.530 --> 01:07:05.760
rock stars wanna be movie stars, my dream is like,

2078
01:07:05.760 --> 01:07:07.690
I always wished I was a standup comic,

2079
01:07:07.690 --> 01:07:10.250
it's the most pure thing in the world.

2080
01:07:10.250 --> 01:07:13.090
You must be approached by CEOs

2081
01:07:13.090 --> 01:07:14.627
and businessmen who are like,

2082
01:07:14.627 --> 01:07:16.620
"I need a little bit of that magic,

2083
01:07:16.620 --> 01:07:19.260
when I go to my next negotiation,

2084
01:07:19.260 --> 01:07:20.960
or where I have to go to this board meeting.

2085
01:07:20.960 --> 01:07:23.780
How do I get people on my page?"

2086
01:07:23.780 --> 01:07:24.613
Right?
Yeah.

2087
01:07:24.613 --> 01:07:27.890
It's sort of tangential to your act,

2088
01:07:27.890 --> 01:07:29.030
and what you do as a mentalist,

2089
01:07:29.030 --> 01:07:32.270
but this skill of understanding people,

2090
01:07:32.270 --> 01:07:36.760
and how to guide them towards this result is very powerful.

2091
01:07:36.760 --> 01:07:40.120
And I think is something that a lot people would pay

2092
01:07:40.120 --> 01:07:42.468
a lot of money to better understand,

2093
01:07:42.468 --> 01:07:45.100
to be like a consultant.

2094
01:07:45.100 --> 01:07:46.549
It's something that I would consider,

2095
01:07:46.549 --> 01:07:49.178
as kind of like an act two, I love performing.

2096
01:07:49.178 --> 01:07:52.660
it fills a void, and it's a rush for me.

2097
01:07:52.660 --> 01:07:53.960
I'm in the corporate space,

2098
01:07:53.960 --> 01:07:56.100
most of my clients are Fortune 500 companies,

2099
01:07:56.100 --> 01:07:57.440
and that's most of what I do.

2100
01:07:57.440 --> 01:07:58.590
You're always wearing a suit,

2101
01:07:58.590 --> 01:07:59.901
it's all very family friendly,

2102
01:07:59.901 --> 01:08:02.260
it's all about making whoever hired

2103
01:08:02.260 --> 01:08:03.726
you look like a superstar,

2104
01:08:03.726 --> 01:08:06.810
that's all very consciously plotted out.

2105
01:08:06.810 --> 01:08:07.643
Fully.

2106
01:08:07.643 --> 01:08:08.670
When I went on, "America's Got Talent",

2107
01:08:08.670 --> 01:08:09.880
I saw it as a commercial.

2108
01:08:09.880 --> 01:08:11.515
They've just given me a TV commercial,

2109
01:08:11.515 --> 01:08:13.260
that if I'm lucky enough,

2110
01:08:13.260 --> 01:08:16.330
will be over 45 minutes of me, maybe even an hour,

2111
01:08:16.330 --> 01:08:18.730
if you add it all up, on primetime TV with millions,

2112
01:08:18.730 --> 01:08:20.110
hundreds of millions of eyeballs,

2113
01:08:20.110 --> 01:08:21.860
what do I want somebody to watch and think?

2114
01:08:21.860 --> 01:08:22.920
'Cause they don't know who I am.

2115
01:08:22.920 --> 01:08:24.160
Right.
And so that show

2116
01:08:24.160 --> 01:08:25.940
is so great at crafting a narrative.

2117
01:08:25.940 --> 01:08:27.650
And for me it was like the Wall Street guy,

2118
01:08:27.650 --> 01:08:28.670
the guy who left Wall Street,

2119
01:08:28.670 --> 01:08:30.610
had a career that should have been very fruitful,

2120
01:08:30.610 --> 01:08:33.320
left it to take a chance on a dream, and then that's it.

2121
01:08:33.320 --> 01:08:35.140
Like I do appeal to do that crowd,

2122
01:08:35.140 --> 01:08:36.470
because honestly I know their industry,

2123
01:08:36.470 --> 01:08:38.690
I know most industries really well, I study.

2124
01:08:38.690 --> 01:08:40.840
If I go in and do something for a company

2125
01:08:40.840 --> 01:08:42.050
that does, you know, finance,

2126
01:08:42.050 --> 01:08:44.610
or if they do some sort of multinational product,

2127
01:08:44.610 --> 01:08:45.840
pharmaceutical, anything,

2128
01:08:45.840 --> 01:08:47.440
I will know their product inside and out,

2129
01:08:47.440 --> 01:08:49.037
to the point where they go,

2130
01:08:49.037 --> 01:08:50.550
"You could work for us."

2131
01:08:50.550 --> 01:08:52.970
That's my goal, is to be somebody on their team,

2132
01:08:52.970 --> 01:08:54.439
not just performing with them...

2133
01:08:54.439 --> 01:08:56.541
But like not for them, but with them.

2134
01:08:56.541 --> 01:08:58.150
So yeah, that was very on purpose

2135
01:08:58.150 --> 01:08:59.800
to do the suit and be corporate,

2136
01:08:59.800 --> 01:09:01.850
just because I don't wanna be edgy.

2137
01:09:01.850 --> 01:09:04.470
I'm not swearing in my shows, or putting people down.

2138
01:09:04.470 --> 01:09:06.390
You're the Jim Gaffigan of mentalists.

2139
01:09:06.390 --> 01:09:10.150
I've worked with Jim, many times, amazing guy, love Jim.

2140
01:09:10.150 --> 01:09:12.010
Well back to "America's Got Talent",

2141
01:09:12.010 --> 01:09:15.790
so you do your six performances, they all go well,

2142
01:09:15.790 --> 01:09:19.205
you end up third, of all those judges though,

2143
01:09:19.205 --> 01:09:21.730
who was the most difficult,

2144
01:09:21.730 --> 01:09:24.400
like who was the biggest challenge among the panel?

2145
01:09:24.400 --> 01:09:26.728
I mean, Howard called you like a dark wizard.

2146
01:09:26.728 --> 01:09:27.760
(laughs)

2147
01:09:27.760 --> 01:09:30.880
So I ran into Howard Stern this summer in Long Island,

2148
01:09:30.880 --> 01:09:32.750
and it was funny because I was out running.

2149
01:09:32.750 --> 01:09:35.200
And he's got a place near me in Southampton,

2150
01:09:35.200 --> 01:09:37.978
and I'm running around, and I see him,

2151
01:09:37.978 --> 01:09:40.600
and he's easy to spy, he's very tall.

2152
01:09:40.600 --> 01:09:42.983
And he's notorious, kind of germophobic,

2153
01:09:42.983 --> 01:09:44.130
and it's COVID, and I didn't wanna go near him,

2154
01:09:44.130 --> 01:09:45.367
but I had to say something,

2155
01:09:45.367 --> 01:09:47.190
and it's actually, we're on a track.

2156
01:09:47.190 --> 01:09:48.847
And I just run by, and I say,

2157
01:09:48.847 --> 01:09:52.510
"Howard, I gotta say, thank you, man, you changed my life."

2158
01:09:52.510 --> 01:09:54.415
And he didn't instant recognize me, but then I go,

2159
01:09:54.415 --> 01:09:55.370
"I was on "America's Got Talent", I was Oz."

2160
01:09:55.370 --> 01:09:56.387
And he knew, he's like, right away he goes,

2161
01:09:56.387 --> 01:09:57.510
"Oh my God, the mentalist."

2162
01:09:57.510 --> 01:09:59.169
He remembered very vividly about it,

2163
01:09:59.169 --> 01:10:00.160
and he was with his wife.

2164
01:10:00.160 --> 01:10:04.110
And he was a few laps over, I walked a lap with them,

2165
01:10:04.110 --> 01:10:05.780
just talking about how much it changed my life.

2166
01:10:05.780 --> 01:10:08.970
Because that show is so different

2167
01:10:08.970 --> 01:10:10.030
than being on any other show.

2168
01:10:10.030 --> 01:10:11.720
If you go on like "Jimmy Fallon",

2169
01:10:11.720 --> 01:10:13.130
or something that traditionally is like,

2170
01:10:13.130 --> 01:10:15.140
you think that's making it,

2171
01:10:15.140 --> 01:10:16.660
people aren't emotionally invested.

2172
01:10:16.660 --> 01:10:18.260
When some of you watch the sport team,

2173
01:10:18.260 --> 01:10:20.370
you have your team that you root for.

2174
01:10:20.370 --> 01:10:21.880
So something about "America's Got Talent",

2175
01:10:21.880 --> 01:10:22.770
the people that like it,

2176
01:10:22.770 --> 01:10:24.780
a lot of people watch it with their family,

2177
01:10:24.780 --> 01:10:26.850
there's not a lot of stuff on TV that transcends ages.

2178
01:10:26.850 --> 01:10:28.190
You can have your six year old,

2179
01:10:28.190 --> 01:10:29.420
and you know it's gonna be appropriate,

2180
01:10:29.420 --> 01:10:31.840
and you could have your 86 year old grandma there.

2181
01:10:31.840 --> 01:10:33.970
And so people decide who their money horse is.

2182
01:10:33.970 --> 01:10:34.803
And early on, a lot of people,

2183
01:10:34.803 --> 01:10:37.530
just got very emotionally invested in me, I don't know.

2184
01:10:37.530 --> 01:10:39.027
And so I'll meet people to this day, who are like,

2185
01:10:39.027 --> 01:10:40.330
"Yo, I voted for you."

2186
01:10:40.330 --> 01:10:44.240
And it it's just wild how much people will root for you.

2187
01:10:44.240 --> 01:10:47.190
And so I think of the judges,

2188
01:10:47.190 --> 01:10:49.420
I had great rapport with everybody.

2189
01:10:49.420 --> 01:10:51.980
I feel like ha Heidi and I had a great dynamic.

2190
01:10:51.980 --> 01:10:53.500
Mel B was a little bit...

2191
01:10:53.500 --> 01:10:55.636
Mel B's hard to crack, because certain people,

2192
01:10:55.636 --> 01:10:58.980
when you say they're kind of a free spirit,

2193
01:10:58.980 --> 01:11:00.690
and you don't know what will happen in the moment.

2194
01:11:00.690 --> 01:11:01.523
And when you're on live TV like that,

2195
01:11:01.523 --> 01:11:02.947
and you ask somebody to think of something, they're like,

2196
01:11:02.947 --> 01:11:04.690
"Oh my God, I don't know."

2197
01:11:04.690 --> 01:11:06.367
And she's changing her mind like eight times.

2198
01:11:06.367 --> 01:11:07.740
And it's not that I mind that,

2199
01:11:07.740 --> 01:11:10.070
'cause I know she's gonna do that, I'm anticipating,

2200
01:11:10.070 --> 01:11:11.760
it's that I'm on a clock.

2201
01:11:11.760 --> 01:11:12.730
And so with people like that,

2202
01:11:12.730 --> 01:11:14.030
I have to create a different dynamic,

2203
01:11:14.030 --> 01:11:15.920
because I need them to stop changing

2204
01:11:15.920 --> 01:11:17.500
their mind where I want them to,

2205
01:11:17.500 --> 01:11:19.160
and she's going on her own tangent.

2206
01:11:19.160 --> 01:11:21.285
And so you have to start creating...

2207
01:11:21.285 --> 01:11:24.480
It's like a game of chess, it's just like chess,

2208
01:11:24.480 --> 01:11:26.010
but I'm playing seven moves in advance

2209
01:11:26.010 --> 01:11:27.770
with somebody that doesn't know I'm playing them.

2210
01:11:27.770 --> 01:11:29.910
And so I'm playing a game of chess

2211
01:11:29.910 --> 01:11:31.130
with somebody where I have to control it,

2212
01:11:31.130 --> 01:11:32.410
and I have to like do something

2213
01:11:32.410 --> 01:11:34.260
that jolt her brain in a way that she stops,

2214
01:11:34.260 --> 01:11:35.300
and we go back to what I need.

2215
01:11:35.300 --> 01:11:36.895
I'm, I don't wanna say it,

2216
01:11:36.895 --> 01:11:37.930
'cause it sounds like a manipulator,

2217
01:11:37.930 --> 01:11:40.960
but I'm controlling what you will do inside your brain

2218
01:11:40.960 --> 01:11:43.990
through a lot of different physical,

2219
01:11:43.990 --> 01:11:46.420
verbal, and non-verbal communications,

2220
01:11:46.420 --> 01:11:47.850
and she's very hard to do that with.

2221
01:11:47.850 --> 01:11:49.800
Yeah, the one kind of standout thing

2222
01:11:49.800 --> 01:11:53.260
that you did with her, was have her write down some place

2223
01:11:53.260 --> 01:11:55.940
that she went on vacation with a certain individual,

2224
01:11:55.940 --> 01:11:57.660
and it's gotta be tricky, because these are celebrities,

2225
01:11:57.660 --> 01:11:59.760
and you can Google this stuff, right?

2226
01:11:59.760 --> 01:12:01.249
So you have to tick something,

2227
01:12:01.249 --> 01:12:06.249
or get them to engage in an experiment

2228
01:12:06.270 --> 01:12:08.290
that's not gonna be anything that's on the internet,

2229
01:12:08.290 --> 01:12:09.694
or discoverable online.

2230
01:12:09.694 --> 01:12:10.570
Right.

2231
01:12:10.570 --> 01:12:11.403
Like, think about this,

2232
01:12:11.403 --> 01:12:12.910
just visualizing something in your brain,

2233
01:12:12.910 --> 01:12:14.064
and where your brain will go...

2234
01:12:14.064 --> 01:12:15.910
You've done Ultramans, right?

2235
01:12:15.910 --> 01:12:17.330
Mm-hmm.
Have you done Ironmans

2236
01:12:17.330 --> 01:12:18.670
as well?
No.

2237
01:12:18.670 --> 01:12:19.830
Never an Ironman, it's so funny,

2238
01:12:19.830 --> 01:12:20.690
jumped right to the big one.

2239
01:12:20.690 --> 01:12:22.300
Yeah.
So what was

2240
01:12:22.300 --> 01:12:24.490
your PR at the Ironman?

2241
01:12:24.490 --> 01:12:25.550
Or the Ultraman, I apologize.

2242
01:12:25.550 --> 01:12:27.400
Do you remember it?
The total time?

2243
01:12:27.400 --> 01:12:29.000
It's consolidated, right?

2244
01:12:29.000 --> 01:12:31.380
It's like 83 days, yeah, the total time,

2245
01:12:31.380 --> 01:12:33.900
I don't know, was like 23, 24 hour,

2246
01:12:33.900 --> 01:12:35.460
I can't remember, I don't know.

2247
01:12:35.460 --> 01:12:36.293
Do this-
I mean,

2248
01:12:36.293 --> 01:12:38.340
I remember some of the individual day times, or, but-

2249
01:12:38.340 --> 01:12:40.062
Imagine this, I don't know if you're PR'ing,

2250
01:12:40.062 --> 01:12:41.704
but this is just visualize, I want you to see this,

2251
01:12:41.704 --> 01:12:42.824
this is the way your brain works.

2252
01:12:42.824 --> 01:12:45.186
Visualize you crossing that finish line,

2253
01:12:45.186 --> 01:12:46.388
and you've done that how many times?

2254
01:12:46.388 --> 01:12:47.647
Twice.
Twice.

2255
01:12:47.647 --> 01:12:49.006
So imagine a third time,

2256
01:12:49.006 --> 01:12:50.156
and now this is in your brain,

2257
01:12:50.156 --> 01:12:51.153
just play this out in your mind,

2258
01:12:51.153 --> 01:12:52.656
I just want you to see how your brain would work on this,

2259
01:12:52.656 --> 01:12:53.628
it's not a trick.

2260
01:12:53.628 --> 01:12:54.886
You cross the finish line-

2261
01:12:54.886 --> 01:12:56.308
You say not a trick?
No, it's not-

2262
01:12:56.308 --> 01:12:57.641
Is there something tied to this?

2263
01:12:57.641 --> 01:12:58.628
I don't trust.
I want you

2264
01:12:58.628 --> 01:13:00.435
to imagine you crossed the finish line,

2265
01:13:00.435 --> 01:13:03.050
and right at that moment, somebody takes a photo of you.

2266
01:13:03.050 --> 01:13:05.153
Now, did you go fast, did you not?

2267
01:13:05.153 --> 01:13:05.986
I don't know how the clock works,

2268
01:13:05.986 --> 01:13:07.560
but tell me a very specific time,

2269
01:13:07.560 --> 01:13:09.520
what would you have seen the time be above your head,

2270
01:13:09.520 --> 01:13:11.250
when you crossed that finish line?

2271
01:13:11.250 --> 01:13:13.340
Would it have been faster than the last one you did,

2272
01:13:13.340 --> 01:13:14.982
or slower?
Faster.

2273
01:13:14.982 --> 01:13:16.090
Right?

2274
01:13:16.090 --> 01:13:16.923
'Cause everybody wants fast,

2275
01:13:16.923 --> 01:13:17.756
are you sure though?

2276
01:13:17.756 --> 01:13:18.750
Are you sure?
Yeah.

2277
01:13:18.750 --> 01:13:21.250
What would the time be, exactly, how many hours?

2278
01:13:22.441 --> 01:13:23.490
You want me to just tell you?

2279
01:13:23.490 --> 01:13:24.390
Yeah, I wanna know how you thought about it.

2280
01:13:24.390 --> 01:13:27.659
So the time would be for the double marathon.

2281
01:13:27.659 --> 01:13:28.760
No, not the double-
